  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Salon de l&#x2019;Agriculture et des Resources Animales (SARA) Start-up mission</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this activity is to include Orange Corners entrepreneurs from C&#xF4;te d&#x2019;Ivoire, Morocco and Senegal in the Salon de l&#x2019;Agriculture et des Resources Animales (SARA) fair and increase the impact of their participation. The SARA fair will be organized in Abidjan.This year, the Netherlands is the chosen country of honour. By providing the Orange Corners start-ups with training, support and better access to markets in preparation for, during and after the SARA, this project will maximize the results of their participation at the fair. Besides, the implementing partner will take care of the logistical support to the entrepreneurs (including visa, flights and hotel booking).This project aims to promote knowledge transfer, trade and regional integration through organizing a start-up trade mission. The secondary aim is to establish possible business relationships, collaborations and networks between the start-ups from the three countries, adding an extra layer to the impact of the current Orange Corners programmes.</narrative>
  </description>
